    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0263" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg213"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smythe to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with the instructions
                    contained in your dispatch No. 8, Santo Domingo series, dated January 13, last,
                    I beg to transmit herewith inclosed copy of a letter received from Juan A. Read,
                    esq., U. S. vice-consul, acting, in reply to my letter to him requesting that an
                    inquiry be made in the matter of the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Lavinia M.
                        Snow</hi> and report the result of such inquiry to this office.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry M. Smythe.</hi></signed></closer>



